= Custom Houdini Procedural =
#context: lop
#type: node

"""Assigns a Houdini Procedural to a specified USD primitive for rendering."""

== Overview ==

Custom Houdini Procedural configures a USD primitive to be rendered using a Houdini Procedural. A Houdini Procedural is a plugin that generates geometry at render time from a SOP graph.

WARNING:
    The Karma/Mantra render command must include the argument `--allowed-procedurals all` unless the procedural outputs only curves or points.

@parameters

Graph File:
    #id: graph_file
    SOP-level graph file provided as input to the procedural.

Procedural Script:
    #id: procedural_script
    The Python script the renderer runs, `invokegraph.py` by default. A bare file name is looked up under `houdiniprocedurals` in `HOUDINI_HUSDPLUGINS_PATH`; a full path is used as is. The renderer skips a script it cannot find without reporting it, so the node reports an error when the same lookup finds nothing on this machine.

    A custom script defines `procedural(prim, args)` and returns a `hou.Geometry` (Houdini 22 also accepts a list of `(time, hou.Geometry)` pairs). `args` holds `graph`, the Graph File; `inputs`, the relationship names on the primitive whose targets are each input's primitives; and `overrides`, mapping each graph parameter to the primvar holding its value.

Procedural Name:
    #id: proc_name
    Name of the registered Houdini Procedural.

Procedural Primitive:
    #id: proc_prim
    The USD primitive to configure as a Houdini Procedural.

Animated Procedural:
    #id: proc_animated
    Run the procedural again before every frame. Off, it runs once before the render starts and every frame uses that result, so turn it off only when nothing the graph reads changes over time, Animated overrides included.

Inputs:
    #id: inputs
    USD primitives to use as inputs to the SOP graph. Each entry is one input and may be a pattern or several primitives; an entry that matches nothing is an error.

Overrides:
    #id: overrides
    Overrides for SOP graph parameters and USD primitive properties.
